class:: EnvelopeKurtosis
summary:: Concentration and tails of envelope energy over time
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Amplitude

description::
The fourth energy-weighted central time moment divided by squared temporal variance. This is Pearson kurtosis, not excess kurtosis; three is Gaussian. Degenerate variance returns zero.

Frames contain nonoverlapping RMS measurements. Output stays zero until a complete observation window is available, then updates once per RMS frame. Silence returns zero. Runtime cost is linear in windowTime/frameTime per update; there is no callback allocation. These descriptors are rolling summaries and do not segment individual events. Formulas are independently implemented from standard weighted moments and linear regression.

The nearest vanilla building block is link::Classes/Amplitude::, which tracks instantaneous level; this UGen summarizes its recent distribution in time.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time observation duration, 2*frameTime through 10 seconds. Rounded up to whole RMS frames.

argument:: frameTime
Initialization-time RMS frame duration, 0.001 through 0.1 seconds.

argument:: floorDB
Silence floor in dBFS, clipped to -160..0. Used by dynamic complexity and dB regression; temporal moments use the original energy.

returns::
Nonnegative dimensionless kurtosis.

examples::
EnvelopeKurtosis computes the fourth energy-weighted temporal moment divided by squared variance (Pearson kurtosis, where 3 represents a Gaussian distribution). Highly impulsive plucked notes generate prominent kurtosis spikes (> 6). In this example, high kurtosis triggers an auxiliary crystalline chime layer, emphasizing crisp transients while leaving smooth sustained segments uncluttered. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time envelope kurtosis.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("plucks.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic pluck fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(1.5);
            var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.4), trig);
            Pluck.ar(WhiteNoise.ar * env, trig, 0.2, 1/220, 2.0, 0.3)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var kurt = EnvelopeKurtosis.kr(source, windowTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005);
        var kurtLag = kurt.lag(0.05);
        var chimeGate = (kurtLag > 6.0).lag(0.01, 0.1);
        var chime = Ringz.ar(K2A.ar(chimeGate) * 0.05, 2400, 0.2) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + (chime ! 2);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, kurtLag.clip(1, 20)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Envelope Kurtosis", ~miraBus, 1.0, 15.0, "kurt");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
